[thin] Outside this pass and reported to Derek: the cold-core stack's shared 2 mm section. The casing is 2.0 mm of wall behind 1.2 mm show flutes, the same section the shell and every cap and lid carry, and each conduit column keeps the shared 2.0 mm wall round its Ø7.5 bore. The readings sit at the flute troughs and on those column walls.
alternatives: A 3 mm casing grows the whole stack's footprint or takes a millimetre a side from the foam, and Derek's printed shell carries the present section. 3 mm conduit walls widen every column by 2 mm, into the 1.5 mm pour gaps the cup keeps beside the casing and between columns. Either is a stack revision, not a local fix.
